        </style></head><body><header><a href="/">CTSMD Connect</a></header><main><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p class="notice"><strong>Draft for review.</strong> Proposed effective date: November 4, 2026. This policy requires CTSMD approval before publication.</p><p>Children’s Theatre of Southern Maryland (CTSMD) operates CTSMD Connect at ctsmd.me and the CTSMD Connect applications for iOS and Android. This policy describes information handled through those services.</p>
        <h2>Information we handle</h2><p>Depending on how you use Connect, information may include account and contact details, dates of birth, family and guardian relationships, production participation, schedules, registration and form responses, messages, community posts, photographs, videos, and other files. Some forms may request allergy or accommodation information. Device notification registration may include a device or push token.</p>
        <h2>How information is used</h2><p>CTSMD uses information to manage accounts and theatre activities; communicate with participants and families; provide schedules, forms and content; support safety and moderation; and administer access and the services. People see information according to their assigned access and relationships.</p>
        <h2>Children, families and safeguarding</h2><p>Connect supports youth theatre participants and their families. CTSMD manages student accounts and guardian relationships, and access to family and student information depends on those relationships and the user’s role. Communications and community content may be reviewed for safety and moderation. Parents and guardians can contact CTSMD with questions about a child’s information.</p>
        <h2>Services and sharing</h2><p>CTSMD may use service providers to operate the website and apps, deliver email or notifications, store or display media, and support ticketing or payment functions where enabled. Your device’s operating system and app store also provide services. Links to other websites and services are governed by their own policies. CTSMD may share information with authorized staff and service providers as needed for their roles and applicable services.</p>
        <h2>Retention and deletion</h2><p>CTSMD retains records for operational, safety, financial, and other applicable purposes. Retention periods and exceptions depend on the type of record and applicable obligations. Contact CTSMD to ask about a particular record, request correction, or request deletion of an account or personal data. CTSMD will review requests and may need to verify identity or authority, including for a child’s information. Some records may need to be retained; CTSMD can explain applicable limits when responding.</p>
        <h2 id="deletion">Request account or data deletion</h2><p>To request deletion of your CTSMD Connect account or associated personal data, use the <a href="https://www.ctsmd.org/">CTSMD website contact form</a>. State that your request concerns CTSMD Connect, identify the account by its email address, and describe the information you want deleted. For a child’s information, identify your relationship to the child; do not include medical details, passwords, or other sensitive information in the initial request. CTSMD may contact you to verify your identity or authority before acting.</p>
        <h2>Contact</h2><p>For privacy questions or requests, contact Children’s Theatre of Southern Maryland through its <a href="https://www.ctsmd.org/">public website contact form</a>.</p><footer><a href="/">CTSMD Connect home</a></footer></main></body></html><?php exit;
